.TH scan_to_array 3 "Version 1.0" "December 2023" "lib/textcode"
.SH NAME
scan_to_array \- Scan and store data into an array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/textcode.h>
.sp
.BI "size_t scan_to_array(size_t (*func)(const char*, char*, size_t*), const char* src, array* dest)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function .BR scan_to_array () scans and stores data into an array. The function takes the following parameters:
.sp
1. A pointer to a scanning function that takes a source string, a destination buffer, and a pointer to the size of the destination buffer, and returns the number of bytes processed from the source string.
2. A pointer to the source string.
3. A pointer to the destination array.
.sp
The function returns the number of bytes processed from the source string.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes processed from the source string.
.SH EXAMPLES
No examples are provided for this function.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B array, str
